        "id": "fd_0376",
        "title": "p-Adic Shadow Rigidity of Integer Linear Rewriting Systems",
        "description": "Conjecture: For any finite terminating rewrite system on integer vectors x \\in \\mathbb{Z}^d whose rules are affine maps x \\mapsto A_ix+b_i with det(A_i)=\\pm 1, if every rewrite sequence from x reaches the same normal form over \\mathbb{Z}/p^k\\mathbb{Z} for all primes p and all k\\le K(d,R), then the system is globally confluent over \\mathbb{Z}. Test: Generate explicit affine-unimodular terminating systems, compute normal forms over many residue rings \\mathbb{Z}/p^k\\mathbb{Z}, and check whether agreement up to the predicted bound K implies unique integer normal forms; a counterexample refutes the conjecture. Impact: This would create a new local-to-global principle for certified rewriting and symbolic computation, linking completion/confluence checking to arithmetic finite-model testing rather than exhaustive critical-pair analysis.",
