        "id": "fd_0375",
        "title": "Arithmetic Monodromy Controls Prime-Dependent Torsion Persistence",
        "description": "Conjecture: There exists an explicit infinite family of filtered simplicial complexes K_n defined over Z together with a finite set of integral filtration parameters such that, for infinitely many primes p, the barcode of persistent homology with coefficients in F_p is not determined by the integral persistent barcode plus the Smith normal forms of all boundary maps at individual filtration levels; instead, the missing information is exactly captured by a prime-sensitive monodromy invariant built from extension data between consecutive persistent modules. Test: Construct candidate families K_n, compute persistent homology over Z and over F_p for many primes, and check whether two filtrations with identical levelwise Smith data but different extension/monodromy data yield different mod-p barcodes for infinitely many p. Refutation occurs if integral levelwise data always suffices. Impact: This would reveal a genuinely new arithmetic layer in persistence, forcing a redesign of algebraic-topological data analysis pipelines and linking persistent homology to arithmetic representation theory.",
