        "id": "fd_0385",
        "title": "Tropicalization Commutes with Persistence for Non-Archimedean Point Clouds",
        "description": "Conjecture: Let X be a finite point cloud in (K^d, ||\u00b7||) over a complete non-Archimedean valued field K, and let Trop(X) \u2282 R^d be its coordinatewise valuation image. For Vietoris\u2013Rips filtrations built from the ultrametric on X and the l_infinity metric on Trop(X), there exists a universal constant c_d depending only on d such that, after rescaling filtration parameters by c_d, the persistence modules H_k(VR_t(X); F_p) and H_k(VR_t(Trop(X)); F_p) are interleaving-equivalent for all k. Test: Compute both filtrations for explicit algebraic families of p-adic point clouds (e.g. roots of sparse polynomials, torsion points on p-adic tori, random finite subsets of O_K^d), and check whether barcodes match up to a bounded interleaving constant independent of sample size and valuation depth; a counterexample with unbounded distortion refutes the conjecture. Impact: This would create a rigorous bridge between tropical geometry and topological data analysis, giving a computable Euclidean proxy for non-Archimedean topology and enabling new algorithms for arithmetic datasets.",
