        "title": "Prime Reciprocity in Persistent Torsion via Matroid Duality",
        "description": "Conjecture: There exists a duality transform on finite filtered CW complexes with integer boundary matrices, induced by filtered cellular duality / matroid dualization of the boundary operator, such that the prime-indexed torsion barcode function of the dual complex determines the original torsion barcode up to a computable involution on birth-death intervals for all but finitely many primes. Test: Compute integer persistent homology and prime-wise torsion barcodes for large families of explicitly dualizable filtered complexes (planar cellulations, simplicial pseudomanifolds, matroid boundary realizations), then compare with the predicted transformed barcode of the dual. Confirmation requires statistically exact agreement outside an explicitly bounded exceptional prime set; a single infinite counterfamily refutes it. Impact: This would reveal a hidden reciprocity law for arithmetic topology in persistence, giving a new compression principle for integer persistent homology and a bridge between duality in topology, matroid theory, and prime-sensitive data analysis.",
